{"patch":{"config":{"title":"Antranig Basman","baseURL":"https://ponder.org.uk","defaultContentLanguage":"en","mainSections":["post","posts"],"author":{"name":"Antranig Basman","website":"/","email":"amb26web@ponder.org.uk","twitter":"amb26ponder"},"params":{"homeTitle":"Antranig Basman","subtitle":"Building habitable technologies","bio":"img/20230209_135356 - bio - cropped.jpg","logo":"img/pond.jpg","favicon":"img/favicon.ico","dateFormat":"January 2, 2006","comments":true,"socialShare":true,"showRelatedPosts":true,"commentsLayer":"beautifulWend.comments.giscus","customCSS":["css/ponder.css"],"mediaIcons":[{"title":"Twitter profile","href":"http://twitter.com/amb26ponder","icon":"fab fa-twitter"},{"title":"Send me a message","href":"mailto:amb26webpage@ponder.org.uk","icon":"fa fa-envelope"},{"title":"Antranig's GitHub profile","href":"http://github.com/amb26","icon":"fab fa-github-alt"},{"title":"My papers on DBLP","href":"https://dblp.org/pid/68/5013.html","icon":"fa fa-university"},{"title":"My LinkedIn profile","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/antranigbasman/","icon":"fab fa-linkedin"}],"giscus":{"repo":"amb26/ponder","repoId":"R_kgDOOKllGA","category":"Announcements","categoryId":"DIC_kwDOOKllGM4CvhAS"}},"menu":{"main":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5},{"name":"Layer Linearisation","parent":"docs","url":"docs/linearisation-algorithm","weight":6},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5},{"name":"Terms","url":"term","weight":5}]}},"features":{"selfHosted":true,"hljs":true}},"pages":[{"kind":"page","type":"page","section":"","title":"My Communities","relPermalink":"/communities/","permalink":"https://ponder.org.uk/communities/","outputPath":"/communities/index.html","params":{"title":"My Communities"},"sourcePath":"content/communities.md","content":"<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://imerss.org\"><img src=\"/img/Arachnoidiscus_schmidtii_web_1-2-scaled.jpg\"/></a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\n  Since 2017 I have been Biodiversity Informatics lead for <a href=\"https://imerss.org/\">IMERSS</a>, the \n  Institute for Multidisciplinary Ecological Research in the Salish Sea. I have been working to help communities\n  with different models for knowledge &mdash; expert naturalists, citizen scientists, and Indigenous individuals and\n  others &mdash; respectfully cooperate to share their knowledge of the natural world and be empowered\n  as stewards of their natural environment. Some visualisations I've produced can be seen on the IMERSS\n  <a href=\"https://imerss.github.io/imerss-bioinfo/\">portal</a>.\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://cifar.ca/ai/ai-and-society/cifar-solution-networks/data-communities-for-inclusion/\" class=\"dci-picture\">\n      <img src=\"/img/dci-logo-white.svg\" />\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nBetween 2022 and 2024 I was a Solutions Network Member for CIFAR's \n<a href=\"https://cifar.ca/ai/ai-and-society/cifar-solution-networks/data-communities-for-inclusion/\">Data Communities for Inclusion</a>\nproject, finding ways that self-employed women in India's SEWA cooperatives could effectively own their own \ntechnological platforms. I developed a very low-cost spreadsheet-driven e-commerce platform for\n<a href=\"https://datacommunities.ca/toolkit/sewa-saamarth-app/\">SEWA Saamarth</a> that allowed the members to advertise and sell vegetable products within the Federation.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://lichen.coop/\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/lichen-logo.png\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nI am affiliated with <a href=\"https://lichen.coop/\">Lichen Community Systems</a>, a Canada-based worker-led cooperative building technologies to support the arts, disability\nand, non-profit and cooperative communities. Under this umbrella I have issued a manifesto for \n<a href=\"https://lichen-community-systems.github.io/knitting-data-communities/\">Knitting Data Communities</a> promoting an\nethic for groups of overlapping communities sharing data that concerns them.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture boxer-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://boxer-project.github.io/\">\n    <img height=\"100px\" src=\"/img/boxer-sunrise-2021-03.png\"/>\n    <img height=\"60px\" src=\"/img/boxer.png\" class=\"boxer-boxer-picture\"/>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\n<a href=\"https://boxer-project.github.io\">Boxer</a> is a highly interesting and ancient programming system which\nclosely conforms to Jonathan Edwards' definition of a <a href=\"/term/substrate\">substrate</a>. In 2022 I chaired the \n2nd international workshop dedicated to Boxer in the form of the \n<a href=\"https://2022.programming-conference.org/home/salon-2022\">Boxer Salon</a> hosted at <a href=\"https://2022.programming-conference.org/\">\nProgramming 2022</a> at Porto. I also maintain a helpful <a href=\"https://boxer-project.github.io/boxer-literature/Thematic%20index/\">index to the Boxer\nliterature</a>.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"community-row\">\n  <div class=\"community-picture\">\n  <a href=\"https://malleable.systems/\" class=\"malleable-picture\">\n      <img src=\"/img/malleable-header.svg\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\">\n    <div>Malleable Systems Collective</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"community-desc\">\nThe <a href=\"https://malleable.systems/\">Malleable Systems Collective</a> believes, as I do, that it should be as easy\nto change software as it is to use it. We believe in widening the circle of those empowered to make decisions about\ntheir own technology, through making it as easy as possible to understand and change it. I am currently taking a break\nfrom the MSC on account of their hard no-AI policy.</a>\n  </div>\n</div>\n","summary":"Since 2017 I have been Biodiversity Informatics lead for IMERSS , the Institute for Multidisciplinary Ecological Research in the Salish Sea. I have been working to help communities with different models for knowledge &amp;mdash; expert naturalists, citizen scientists, and Indigenous individuals and others &amp;mdash; respectfully cooperate to share their knowledge of the natural world and be empowered as stewards of their natural environment. Some visualisations I've produced can be seen on the IMERSS portal .","summaryText":"Since 2017 I have been Biodiversity Informatics lead for IMERSS , the Institute for Multidisciplinary Ecological Research in the Salish Sea. I have been working to help communities with different models for knowledge &mdash; expert naturalists, citizen scientists, and Indigenous individuals and others &mdash; respectfully cooperate to share their knowledge of the natural world and be empowered as stewards of their natural environment. Some visualisations I've produced can be seen on the IMERSS portal .","truncated":true,"prevInSection":{"title":"Edit in Infusion - Privacy Policy","relPermalink":"/edit-in-infusion-privacy/"}}],"shared":{"lang":"en","menu":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Docs","id